// Policy 4 of 7 -- "Cumulative budget cap per trajectory".
// From "Securing AI agents with temporal policies in Amazon Bedrock AgentCore", AWS Machine
// Learning Blog, 06 AUG 2026. The policy below is the article's listing VERBATIM, copied byte
// for byte from the published page on 2026-10-02 (reference/README.md has the provenance).
//
// THE ARTICLE'S STATED INTENT:
//   Total trade value in a single policy session (or trajectory) cannot exceed $60,000.
//
// NOTE what the policy sums: the `cost` of get_market_price REQUESTS -- quotes, not trades --
// and that it is a PERMIT, so with no quotes at all the total is 0 and it grants. See
// README.md, findings 1 and 4.

permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (total: Long). ((sum amount for (amount: Long), (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 24h (
        AgentCore::Action::"get_market_price"::request{input.cost: amount, eventResource: resource} && tp(t)))) == total && total < 60000
    )
};
